Article 8 (Metropolitan Transport Operations Bureau)
(1) The Metropolitan Transport Operations Bureau shall have one Director General, who shall be appointed from among general service public officials belonging to the Senior Executive Service.
(2) The Director General shall take charge of the following matters:
1. Construction and operation of metropolitan transport facilities;
2. Expansion of congested roads and metropolitan road facilities in metropolitan areas;
3. Support for metropolitan railway projects implemented by local governments;
4. Approval of establishment and amendment of basic plans for urban railways in metropolitan areas;
5. Construction, management, and support of urban railways in metropolitan areas;
6. Establishment and implementation of comprehensive plans for bus rapid transit systems;
7. Construction, management, and support of bus rapid transit systems;
8. Improvement of the bus rapid transit system and technology development;
9. General coordination of basic plans for construction of transfer centers and complex transfer centers;
10. Construction, management, and support of transfer centers and complex transfer centers;
11. Designation and approval of transfer centers and complex transfer centers;
12. Improvement of transfer convenience at transfer centers and complex transfer centers;
13. Construction and operation of transfer centers supporting environmentally friendly vehicles;
14. Construction and support of bus information systems and transfer information systems in metropolitan areas.
